<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib59.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2504.14286</em>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib60" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhou et al. (2022)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Xiaoling Zhou, Ou Wu, Weiyao Zhu, and Ziyang Liang. 2022.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-26409-2_5" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Understanding difficulty-based sample weighting with a universal difficulty measure</a>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <em id="bib.bib60.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Machine Learning and Knowledge Discovery in Databases - European Conference, ECML PKDD 2022, Grenoble, France, September 19-23, 2022, Proceedings, Part III</em>, volume 13715 of <em id="bib.bib60.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Lecture Notes in Computer Science</em>, pages 68–84. Springer.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Integrated Pipeline with Our LPPO</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section details the integrated progressive opptimization RLVR pipeline that combines PG-Sampling and LP-Weighting to improve sample efficiency and training dynamics. The full algorithm is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Integrated Pipeline with Our LPPO ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Integrated Training Process with Proposed LPPO</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Standard RLVR dataset <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, PG-sampling subset <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{pg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{pg}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial policy parameters <math id="algx1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, EMA decay <math id="algx1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, LP-weighting sensitivity <math id="algx1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, LP-weighting bias <math id="algx1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Updated policy parameters <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 1. Initialize EMA of pass rates</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          Initialize EMA of pass rates <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{p_{i}}(0)\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{p_{i}}(0)\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all samples <math id="algx1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> epoch <math id="algx1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algx1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 2. Compute pass rates</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sample <math id="algx1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="algx1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\cup\mathcal{D}_{pg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\cup\mathcal{D}_{pg}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Roll out current policy <math id="algx1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> on sample <math id="algx1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to compute <math id="algx1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>rate</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             Compute reward <math id="algx1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for trajectories from sample <math id="algx1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="algx1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>rate</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
               Add these trajectories (with reward <math id="algx1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) to the <math id="algx1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="batch" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">batch</annotation></semantics></math> for policy update

</div>
<div id="algx1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 3. PG-Sampling for difficult samples</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sample <math id="algx1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="algx1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{pg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{pg}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algx1.l15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>rate</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             Generate a prefix <math id="algx1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{pre},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mtext>pre</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{pre},i}</annotation></semantics></math> for sample <math id="algx1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> according to Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Prefix-Guided Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Eq. <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Prefix-Guided Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
             Generate the remaining sequence (suffix) <math id="algx1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{rem},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mtext>rem</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{rem},i}</annotation></semantics></math> for this prefix using Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Prefix-Guided Sampling ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
             Compute reward <math id="algx1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for trajectories from sample <math id="algx1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
             Add these prefix-guided trajectories (<math id="algx1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{rem},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mtext>rem</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{rem},i}</annotation></semantics></math>, with reward <math id="algx1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) to the <math id="algx1.l19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="batch" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">batch</annotation></semantics></math> for policy update

</div>
<div id="algx1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 4. Update pass-rate statistics and LP weights</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sample <math id="algx1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="algx1.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="batch" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">batch</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
            
            
             Update EMA of pass rate: <math id="algx1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{p_{i}}(t)\leftarrow(1-\alpha)\overline{p_{i}}(t-1)+\alpha\,\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>pass</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>rate</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{p_{i}}(t)\leftarrow(1-\alpha)\overline{p_{i}}(t-1)+\alpha\,\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l23.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> (Corresponds to Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.3 Learning-Progress Weighting ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
            
            
             Compute learning progress: <math id="algx1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(t)\leftarrow\overline{p_{i}}(t)-\overline{p_{i}}(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(t)\leftarrow\overline{p_{i}}(t)-\overline{p_{i}}(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l24.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> (Corresponds to Eq. <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.3 Learning-Progress Weighting ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
            
            
             Compute LP-weight: <math id="algx1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(t)\leftarrow\sigma(\kappa\cdot\Delta_{i}(t))+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(t)\leftarrow\sigma(\kappa\cdot\Delta_{i}(t))+b</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l25.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> (Corresponds to Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 Learning-Progress Weighting ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, where <math id="algx1.l25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the sigmoid function)
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 5. Compute weighted advantages</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sample <math id="algx1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and rollout index <math id="algx1.l28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
            
            
             Weight the advantage: <math id="algx1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{\prime}_{i,k}\leftarrow w_{i}(t)\,\hat{A}_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{\prime}_{i,k}\leftarrow w_{i}(t)\,\hat{A}_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l29.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> (Corresponds to Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Learning-Progress Weighting ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 6. Policy update</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">32:</span>
            
            
            Update policy <math id="algx1.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> via GRPO <span id="algx1.l32.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> (Corresponds to Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.3 Learning-Progress Weighting ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">33:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// 7. Online data curation</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">34:</span>
            
            
            Remove (or skip) consistently solved samples (with <math id="algx1.l34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>rate</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pass\_rate}_{i}(t)=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>) in <math id="algx1.l34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\cup\mathcal{D}_{pg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\cup\mathcal{D}_{pg}</annotation></semantics></math> from training

</div>
<div id="algx1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">35:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l35.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiment Settings</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same template as Qwen-MATH <span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
              
            https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct</span></span></span>, shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Prompt ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiment Settings ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, for our training and evaluation. For PG-sampling, which combines the solution and the problem for difficult questions, we inject the prefix <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">solution_prefix</span> into the prompt for training, as shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Prompt ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiment Settings ‣ From Data-Centric to Sample-Centric: Enhancing LLM Reasoning via Progressive Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="157.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 157.75" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,157.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.98 L 0 148.77 C 0 153.73 4.02 157.75 8.98 157.75 L 644.17 157.75 C 649.13 157.75 653.15 153.73 653.15 148.77 L 653.15 8.98 C 653.15 4.02 649.13 0 644.17 0 L 8.98 0 C 4.02 0 0 4.02 0 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 8.98 L 1.11 135.47 L 652.04 135.47 L 652.04 8.98 C 652.04 4.63 648.52 1.11 644.17 1.11 L 8.98 1.11 C 4.63 1.11 1.11 4.63 1.11 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 136.58 L 1.11 148.77 C 1.11 153.11 4.63 156.64 8.98 156.64 L 644.17 156.64 C 648.52 156.64 652.04 153.11 652.04 148.77 L 652.04 136.58 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 143.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.18" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="531.9"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:38.44em;">
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 16.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.2em;--ltx-fo-height:7.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="110.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 107.29)" width="611.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.2em;">
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">system</code><span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please reason step by step, and put</code></span>
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">your final answer within \\boxed{}.</code></span>
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">user</code><span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">{question}</code><span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.5.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">assistant</code><span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.6.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">{answer}</code><span id="A2.F5.pic1.2.7.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Prompt template.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.F6.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="157.86" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 157.86" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,157.86) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.98 L 0 148.88 C 0 153.84 4.02 157.86 8.98 157.86 L 644.17 157.86 C 649.13 157.86 653.15 153.84 653.15 148.88 L 653.15 8.98 C 653.15 4.02 649.13 0 644.17 0 L 8.98 0 C 4.02 0 0 4.02 0 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 8.98 L 1.11 135.47 L 652.04 135.47 L 652.04 8.98 C 652.04 4.63 648.52 1.11 644.17 1.11 L 8.98 1.11 C 4.63 1.11 1.11 4.63 1.11 8.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 136.58 L 1.11 148.88 C 1.11 153.23 4.63 156.75 8.98 156.75 L 644.17 156.75 C 648.52 156.75 652.04 153.23 652.04 148.88 L 652.04 136.58 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 143.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="531.9"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:38.44em;">
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt For PG-Sampling</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 16.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.2em;--ltx-fo-height:7.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="110.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 107.29)" width="611.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.2em;">
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">system</code><span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please reason step by step, and put</code></span>
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">your final answer within \\boxed{}.</code></span>
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">user</code><span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.4.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">{question}</code><span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.5.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">assistant</code><span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.6.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><code id="A2.F6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">{solution_prefix} + {answer}</code><span id="A2.F6.pic1.2.7.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Prompt template for PG-Sampling.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward Design</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We focus exclusively on the model’s reasoning ability, not on exposing its entire chain of thought; hence we do not adopt the format reward for Deepseek-R1  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
To minimise the risk of reward-hacking that can arise from elaborate scoring schemes, we employ a deliberately minimal, rule-based metric.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The sole component is mathematical correctness, denoted <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{math}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>math</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{math}}</annotation></semantics></math>; no extra credit is awarded for formatting or auxiliary details.
After the model produces its final answer, an automatic verifier checks equivalence with the ground truth:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{math}}=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if the answer is completely correct},\\[4.0pt]
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>math</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if the answer is completely correct</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{math}}=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if the answer is completely correct},\\[4.0pt]
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Accordingly, the total reward is simply</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
